=c,\n$$\n\nthe trapezoidal method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(2).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=2$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{2-0}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the trapezoidal method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & =\\frac{1}{2}({y}^{′}+{y}_{\\text{new}}^{′})\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((x+y)+({x}_{\\text{new}}+{y}_{\\text{new}}))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y)+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{1}{2}(x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(1)$ and $y(2).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+1=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y \\\\  & =0+1+3\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=1,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=1+1=2.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =x+{x}_{\\text{new}}+3y \\\\  & =1+2+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\ny(1)≈1.00,\\,y(2)≈6.00.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321603 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321603 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321603 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b3b25a9-06c9-5f41-a968-8e309293d9f8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321716 #edb/ref 1080 "-2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321716 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321716 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "482d4f1f-144b-5a7b-9de9-9c2ad029db70" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321793 #edb/ref 1080 "${f}_{min}=0$ and ${f}_{max}=25$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321793 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321793 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "51e8f2b2-e881-54be-8bfe-5a90a63da983" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321843 #edb/ref 1080 "${f}_{min}=-5$ and ${f}_{max}=5$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321843 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321843 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "58776b4d-dfad-5418-8461-511cc2520627" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321978 #edb/ref 1080 "${f}_{min}=-1$ and ${f}_{max}=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321978 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321978 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6a96826c-9c27-5fd9-82e2-7b681ef6be75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322333 #edb/ref 1080 "${f}_{min}=-1$ and ${f}_{max}=5$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322333 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322333 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "94d8e7cb-be9a-518f-a277-ee731c13382d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322675 #edb/ref 1080 "1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322675 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322675 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c4d6378f-0db9-5f1e-8409-7cce5146a925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322763 #edb/ref 1080 "2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322763 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 175921860